Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:06.640
Frozen 2 takes fans deep into the unknown
finally revealing the origin of Elsa's powers,

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.260
Anna's future in Arendelle and the truth about
what happened to the sisters' parents on that

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.260
sea voyage.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.840
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video we'll be discussing the epic ending

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:22.159
of Frozen 2 and how the new movie's mythology
changes everything about the past and future

00:00:22.159 --> 00:00:23.689
for Elsa and Anna.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:27.140
And to celebrate the release of the film,
I'm kicking off a new giveaway!

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.519
For a chance to win, subscribe and keep watching
for more details.

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:35.110
There will, of course, be spoilers for Frozen
2, so take care if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:40.270
When Frozen 2 begins, three years have passed
since the castle gates were opened and Anna,

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.690
the quintessential fairy tale character, is
still basking in her Happily Ever After from

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.760
the first movie.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.780
"Do you ever worry about the notion that nothing
is permanent?"

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.760
"Err, no!"

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.440
And although deep down Anna doesn't want anything
to change as she demonstrates in the song

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.970
"Some Things Never Change", the irony of the
song's title is that nothing could be further

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:02.420
from the truth.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.780
Elsa is the catalyst for change when one night
she goes outside the castle to explore the

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.880
mysterious voice from the north that keeps
calling to her.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.790
Her song "Into The Unknown" reveals the inner
turmoil Elsa feels.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:19.030
At first, she resists the "siren song" because
she knows that answering it will risk everything

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.090
and everyone she loves in Arendelle.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.619
The voice challenges her though because it
understands that Elsa's true destiny is not

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:29.060
to be Queen of Arendelle, but to become something
else.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.999
As Elsa realizes she can't suppress her true
calling any longer, she reaches out to the

00:01:33.999 --> 00:01:34.999
voice.

00:01:34.999 --> 00:01:39.159
The spirits answer back though with dramatic
effect and throw Arendelle into disarray as

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:44.020
the earth and wind upturn the streets and
blow the inhabitants out of the kingdom and

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.840
up onto the cliffs.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.929
This event sets Elsa, Anna, Olaf and Kristoff
off on their quest to the Enchanted Lands

00:01:50.929 --> 00:01:53.369
in search of answers to the past.

00:01:53.369 --> 00:01:55.969
"Find who is calling to you.

00:01:55.969 --> 00:01:57.710
They may have answers."

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:02.090
As they part the mist guarding the entrance
to the forest, Olaf remarks that an Enchanted

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:07.340
Forest "is a place of transformation" and
as we'll see all four characters will undergo

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.640
a significant change after their time there.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:15.360
Inside the forest, the gang meets the Arendellians
and Northuldra people who were trapped inside

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.780
when the spirits were angered, and they also
learn that Elsa and Anna's parents met as

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.820
children in the forest.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:26.980
Elsa also discovers her mother's secret connection
to Ahtohallan when Honeymaren explains that

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:31.830
the four symbols on Iduna's scarf represent
each of the four spirits and therefore Iduna's

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.270
connection to nature.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:38.050
A darker secret about Elsa and Anna's parents
is also revealed when the sisters come across

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.780
the wreckage of their ship.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.850
When Elsa extracts the memories of what happened
to the ship from the water soaked into the

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:48.710
wood, they learn that their parents didn't
perish in the Southern Seas as assumed, but

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:53.860
that they were travelling to Ahtohallan in
search of answers about Elsa's powers.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:58.750
The lullaby "All Is Found" is actually Iduna's
"secret message to Elsa" and it contains all

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:02.030
the answers about the themes of the movie
and Elsa's destiny.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:07.420
"When I was little, my mother would sing a
song about a special river called Ahtohallan..

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.850
that was said to hold all the answers about
the past..

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.570
about what we are a part of."

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:17.711
Ahtohallan is the "river full of memory" which
contains the answers to the past that Elsa

00:03:17.711 --> 00:03:19.210
is looking for.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:23.190
And so she goes to the shores of the Dark
Sea which she must cross to find that river

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.960
from the lullaby.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.780
After Elsa tames the water spirit, which appears
as a horse that challenges her to prove herself

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:34.720
worthy, she rides it to Ahtohallan, recalling
the line from "All Is Found", "Come my darling

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.000
homeward bound".

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.770
Ahtohallan is where Elsa's transformation
will occur.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:44.150
She begins to sing "Show Yourself" as she
becomes overjoyed at finding the place she

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.230
truly belongs.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:50.760
Her hair flows loose and free of any constraints
and as she enters into the depths of the frozen

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:55.569
glacier, images of her mother appear in the
ice and both Iduna and the voice sing back

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:56.790
to Elsa.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:01.620
As foretold in the lullaby "All Is Found",
"[Ahtohallan] will sing to those who'll hear

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.780
And in her song, all magic flows."

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:09.380
As she travels deeper into the heart of the
frozen river, Elsa finally reaches the symbols

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:14.130
of the four spirits and embracing the mythical
magical moment, in the centre of the four

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:19.790
symbols a star forms, a symbol or sign of
the fifth spirit which is a union of all four

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:20.880
spirits.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:26.530
This is very much Elsa's new "Let It Go" moment
and as she steps into the centre of the star

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:31.150
it calls back to when she stamped her foot
on the North Mountain and created a giant

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:34.720
snowflake that grew into an enormous Ice Palace.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:40.210
And just like in "Let It Go" when Elsa created
a new blue dress for herself, in "Show Yourself",

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:44.990
Elsa's transformation is completed as her
magic creates a stunning new white flowing

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.260
dress.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:50.830
This is an amazing moment for Elsa, and as
the fifth spirit, her powers are tremendous,

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:54.600
but as we will see she's not invincible.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:59.320
Ahtohallan opens up the memories of the past
and, as Elsa goes deeper and deeper into that

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:04.320
past, she gets colder and colder as she discovers
her grandfather's betrayal of the Northuldra

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.480
people.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:11.030
Elsa's horror and fear and guilt at uncovering
this secret history proves too much and she

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:14.520
literally freezes up with each memory she
uncovers.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:19.250
In the end, as the lullaby "All Is Found"
warned, Elsa dives too deep into this frozen

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:23.350
river of memories and she drowns in ice as
the cold overcomes her.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:28.240
So, in a change from the first film, apparently
the cold does bother Elsa anyway.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.340
Fortunately, as previously explained by Honeymaren,
the Fifth Spirit is also a bridge between

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:38.880
two worlds and to prove this point just before
freezing over, Elsa sends a ray of magic to

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:42.139
her sister Anna who's sheltering in a cave
at that moment.

00:05:42.139 --> 00:05:47.590
The ice magic reveals the truth about their
grandfather to Anna who realizes what she

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:52.260
must do to right the historic wrong the Arendellians
committed against the Northuldra.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:57.350
Anna uses the Earth Giants to destroy the
dam that her treacherous grandfather built,

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:01.660
which lifts the curse the spirits had put
on the Enchanted Forest and also frees Elsa

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.050
from her frozen state.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.300
"Promise me we'll do this together, OK?"

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.300
"I promise."

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:11.100
In the end then, both Anna and Elsa were needed
to break the curse and restore balance to

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.100
the world.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.040
Because, as Elsa points out, their mother
had two daughters.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:20.050
In fact, Anna's heroic moment was foreshadowed
right at the very beginning of the film when

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:23.260
young Elsa and Anna play with a mini enchanted
forest.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:28.810
At the end of their game, Elsa has their fairy
queen toy break the spell, saving everyone,

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.330
and Anna adds that everyone gets married.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:35.730
Based on the previous films you'd probably
associate the magical Elsa with the fairy

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:37.200
queen toy they play with.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:41.320
However, what happens when the girls grow
up is that it's Anna, who although not magical

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:46.180
herself is able to harness the magic of nature
like her Northuldra relatives used to do and

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:51.229
by doing so saves everyone by getting the
earth spirits to take out the dam.

00:06:51.229 --> 00:06:56.310
With Elsa unleashed, we now get to witness
the Avatar or goddess-like powers that she

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.310
commands.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.639
With Arendelle under threat from the dam's
flood waters, Elsa summons and commands the

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:06.410
water spirit, riding it to Arendelle where
she stops and then dissipates the tidal wave

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.630
about to submerge the kingdom.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:13.280
Now there's a lot more to discuss about Elsa's
tremendous new powers in Frozen 2 and I'll

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.770
link to my full video on that here and in
the video description.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.780
After saving Arendelle, Elsa has an emotional
reunion with her sister Anna.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.960
And echoing her "Do you wanna build a snowman?"

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:29.199
phrase from the first movie, Elsa resurrects
Olaf from the pile of snowflakes that he transformed

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:30.199
into.

00:07:30.199 --> 00:07:35.090
Olaf faded away at the same time that Elsa
became frozen in Ahtohallan, because as we

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:39.810
know from the first film, the magical snowman
was the result of Elsa's powers, so when she

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.150
passed, he did too.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:45.900
Fortunately, because water retains memory,
as Olaf tells everyone during the movie, the

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:49.110
little snowman is restored with all of his
previous memories.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:55.810
"The water that makes up you and me has passed
through at least four animals before us."

00:07:55.810 --> 00:08:00.150
With her newfound sense of identity, Elsa
also makes the momentous decision and change

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:05.070
to remain in the north and not return to live
in Arendelle, agreeing with Honeymaren's suggestion

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:06.970
that Elsa belongs there.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:11.790
Now part of Elsa's decision to remain in the
north involves asking Anna to take over from

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:14.430
her as ruler and Queen of Arendelle.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:18.699
Fans will no doubt debate this change of ruler,
but it most likely works out best for both

00:08:18.699 --> 00:08:21.930
sisters and was hinted at early in the movie.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:26.300
After Arendelle was evacuated and GranPabbie
offered to look after the Arendellians, it

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:31.500
was Anna who displayed leadership and took
charge of giving orders to the troll leader:

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.550
"I will look after your people."

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:36.210
"Please make sure they stay out of the kingdom
until we return."

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:37.380
"Of course."

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:41.110
This isn't to take anything away from Elsa,
it's just that Anna is better suited to the

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:45.790
more constrained and human side of being in
charge of a kingdom whereas Elsa's magical

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:50.480
abilities and sense of mythic destiny mean
she's better suited to live near nature where

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:55.460
she can freely make use of her magic without
causing problems to those around her.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:09:00.010
Ultimately, Elsa has never felt fully at ease
in Arendelle and her quest to Ahtohallan has

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.460
shown her where she truly belongs.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:07.010
On the other hand, Anna is perfectly suited
to life in Arendelle, and at the end, both

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.670
set a regular date to meet up at the castle
every week.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:13.140
"Never a dull moment with you two."

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:17.170
Another huge change for Anna is that by end
of the movie, Kristoff finally manages to

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:20.610
make his proposal to her and they get married.

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:24.630
And on the subject of Anna and her Happily
Ever After ending, we need to jump back a

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:29.610
moment and talk about her transformation after
she was separated from Elsa and ended up alone

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:31.670
in a cave with Olaf.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:36.210
After Anna receives the message from her sister
about their grandfather and the dam, Olaf

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:40.740
begins to flurry away and he sadly reveals
to Anna that if the magic is fading from him,

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.450
then her sister must not be OK either.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:47.790
Anna then goes through the heart-breaking
moment of holding her snowman friend in her

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:52.070
arms as he fades into snowflakes, knowing
this also meant her sister's life-force was

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:53.260
also fading.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:58.660
For Anna who's an eternal optimist and started
the movie in such a happy place, these losses

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.880
are heavy blows that send her into a deep
sadness.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:07.220
Still, she manages to draw on her inner strength
and pull herself out of the depths of despair

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:09.420
with her song "The Next Right Thing".

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:13.900
As Anna sings this emotional song, she determines
that she can survive and get through it by

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:17.390
moving forward one small step at a time.

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:21.580
Through this transformation, Anna matures
into a more complex character which makes

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:24.790
her even better suited to be the new Queen
of Arendelle.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.640
And her sister Elsa is now truly at peace
with her powers.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:33.410
To learn all about Elsa's new abilities and
exactly what she can now do after Frozen 2,

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:37.959
tap here or click the link in the video description
to watch my full breakdown of all of Elsa's

00:10:37.959 --> 00:10:39.010
new powers.

